WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:06.720
The racers were ready at dawn.

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:07.863
Very tense.

00:00:10.740 --> 00:00:13.500
In some circles, King
of the Hammers is a far

00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:17.370
far better thing than the
Super Bowl, the Kentucky Derby

00:00:17.370 --> 00:00:20.763
and a Kim Kardashian NFT
drop, all rolled into one.

00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:25.290
This race attracts a very special breed.

00:00:25.290 --> 00:00:27.300
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa.

00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:28.133
Piss off.

00:00:34.680 --> 00:00:36.480
It was time to get grounded

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:38.400
to ponder this rotten assignment

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:40.800
and figure out how to cope with it.

00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:43.410
Seven days in the deep desert surrounded

00:00:43.410 --> 00:00:45.108
by madness and anarchy.

00:00:45.108 --> 00:00:46.166
King of Hammers.

00:00:46.166 --> 00:00:47.850
It's race day you all.

00:00:47.850 --> 00:00:49.350
Hell, even the grandmas here

00:00:49.350 --> 00:00:52.083
make Burning Man look
like a bunch of grandmas.

00:00:55.530 --> 00:00:57.420
Those of us who had been up all night were

00:00:57.420 --> 00:01:00.510
in no mood for lattes and sausage rolls.

00:01:00.510 --> 00:01:02.610
We wanted strong drink.

00:01:02.610 --> 00:01:05.010
We were after all the absolute cream

00:01:05.010 --> 00:01:07.980
of internet travel log influencers.

00:01:07.980 --> 00:01:10.440
We were gathered here in the
desert of Johnson Valley,

00:01:10.440 --> 00:01:13.440
California to witness
the spirit of invention

00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:15.123
in its most feral form.

00:01:16.110 --> 00:01:18.270
When it comes to a thing like this,

00:01:18.270 --> 00:01:19.443
you don't fool around.

00:01:42.450 --> 00:01:45.903
The man driving this beast of
a vehicle is Shannon Campbell.

00:01:47.100 --> 00:01:49.950
He's 53, has very poor vision

00:01:49.950 --> 00:01:52.593
and has won King of the
Hammers, three times.

00:01:54.480 --> 00:01:57.180
He's an absolute racing legend.

00:01:57.180 --> 00:01:58.893
And you're about to see why.

00:02:07.080 --> 00:02:07.950
Look at Shannon.

00:02:07.950 --> 00:02:10.410
A complete roll lands on the tires and

00:02:10.410 --> 00:02:11.793
keeps on going.

00:02:12.840 --> 00:02:14.430
You or I might be traumatized

00:02:14.430 --> 00:02:16.533
by a near death experience like that,

00:02:18.990 --> 00:02:20.940
but not Shannon.

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:22.320
Had a good run going up on top

00:02:22.320 --> 00:02:25.770
and I stuffed it and it kicked

00:02:25.770 --> 00:02:27.300
the fuel pump out or something.

00:02:27.300 --> 00:02:28.276
What about when you flipped?

00:02:28.276 --> 00:02:29.796
That was crazy.

00:02:29.796 --> 00:02:31.315
I screwed up, I was,

00:02:31.315 --> 00:02:32.970
Oh, is that scary though? It's got to be.

00:02:32.970 --> 00:02:36.660
No, I mean, scary is when it doesn't

00:02:36.660 --> 00:02:39.793
get landed on its wheels.

00:02:44.490 --> 00:02:45.690
Things you should know about

00:02:45.690 --> 00:02:46.863
King of the Hammers.

00:02:48.960 --> 00:02:50.820
It's a 10 day event that takes place

00:02:50.820 --> 00:02:52.563
in the Southern California desert.

00:02:53.460 --> 00:02:54.930
There are a series of races

00:02:54.930 --> 00:02:57.123
for different types of off-road vehicles.

00:02:58.200 --> 00:03:03.200
Also, mayhem, chaos and very few rules.

00:03:03.750 --> 00:03:05.313
Totally normal thing to do.

00:03:06.810 --> 00:03:09.813
This year, 80,000 maniacs attended.

00:03:12.060 --> 00:03:14.380
Revelries commence with the time trials

00:03:17.580 --> 00:03:19.950
and climax with the Race of Kings.

00:03:19.950 --> 00:03:24.270
A 200 mile course that requires
drivers to conquer rocks

00:03:24.270 --> 00:03:28.170
and to drive at incredibly
high speeds across the desert.

00:03:28.170 --> 00:03:29.940
It's basically impossible.

00:03:29.940 --> 00:03:33.093
So it attracts the kind of
people who like impossible.

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:38.160
People like Bailey Campbell, who headed

00:03:38.160 --> 00:03:41.970
into race week as a serious
contender for the Crown.

00:03:41.970 --> 00:03:43.680
I got my whole family out here.

00:03:43.680 --> 00:03:46.170
My dad, my brother, my husband.

00:03:46.170 --> 00:03:47.670
How many years have you done this?

00:03:47.670 --> 00:03:49.165
This will be my eighth King of the Hammers

00:03:49.165 --> 00:03:50.193
Eighth. Okay.

00:03:52.080 --> 00:03:54.870
The Campbell's are a racing family.

00:03:54.870 --> 00:03:57.090
There's Bailey's brother Wayland.

00:03:57.090 --> 00:03:58.790
And you've already met Dad, Shannon

00:04:00.150 --> 00:04:03.120
and she married a fellow
speed fiend as well.

00:04:03.120 --> 00:04:04.945
Is that your husband, back from the track?

00:04:04.945 --> 00:04:06.510
Yeah.

00:04:06.510 --> 00:04:08.490
Money.
It was so smooth.

00:04:08.490 --> 00:04:09.660
I got it by six seconds.

00:04:09.660 --> 00:04:11.670
Oh
We watched it, yeah.

00:04:11.670 --> 00:04:15.030
For Bailey though things
aren't going so smoothly

00:04:15.030 --> 00:04:17.850
with only a few precious
days before the big race,

00:04:17.850 --> 00:04:19.320
Bailey has just found out

00:04:19.320 --> 00:04:22.110
that her vehicle is in need of big fixes.

00:04:22.110 --> 00:04:24.990
I mean I know vehicles are
always kind of fickle and every

00:04:24.990 --> 00:04:25.823
this is normal or,

00:04:25.823 --> 00:04:28.358
Probably, no, no.

00:04:28.358 --> 00:04:30.930
It's not.
Nope, this probably

00:04:30.930 --> 00:04:32.665
the worst repair we've had to do all year.

00:04:32.665 --> 00:04:33.498
Yeah.

00:04:33.498 --> 00:04:35.460
I will call you later tonight
when you guys are ready

00:04:35.460 --> 00:04:38.790
to go through UTB parts
to disperse through pits.

00:04:38.790 --> 00:04:41.160
You're going to run home, try to fix it

00:04:41.160 --> 00:04:42.690
and then try to get back by Friday.

00:04:42.690 --> 00:04:44.370
Yeah. Yeah.

00:04:44.370 --> 00:04:45.510
Wish you a lot of luck.

00:04:45.510 --> 00:04:46.783
Get back here.

00:04:46.783 --> 00:04:48.027
Thank you.
Okay, thanks.

00:04:48.027 --> 00:04:50.460
And just like that, Bailey is wondering

00:04:50.460 --> 00:04:52.323
if she'll even be able to race.

00:04:54.120 --> 00:04:58.140
A lot of the competitors are
like her, passionate, scrappy,

00:04:58.140 --> 00:04:59.890
barely holding their cars together.

00:05:01.020 --> 00:05:03.720
Then there are folks like Jason Scherer.

00:05:03.720 --> 00:05:05.340
We have enough ground
clearance to literally

00:05:05.340 --> 00:05:08.910
get our tire between this rock,

00:05:08.910 --> 00:05:09.813
and this.

00:05:10.830 --> 00:05:13.350
Jason is one of this year's favorites.

00:05:13.350 --> 00:05:16.593
Like Shannon, he's won King
of the Hammers three times.

00:05:17.700 --> 00:05:21.210
75% of people don't finish this race.

00:05:21.210 --> 00:05:24.060
Finishing it's an monumental task,

00:05:24.060 --> 00:05:24.960
And an achievement.

00:05:24.960 --> 00:05:26.190
Right? And you feel good after if

00:05:26.190 --> 00:05:28.140
you do it, but once you've won it,

00:05:28.140 --> 00:05:29.580
finishing it is no longer the goal,

00:05:29.580 --> 00:05:31.233
it's only winning it again.

00:05:32.820 --> 00:05:35.670
If the Campbells are a DIY family affair,

00:05:35.670 --> 00:05:40.140
Jason is a polished professional
with money, a big team,

00:05:40.140 --> 00:05:42.210
and a decked out vehicle.

00:05:42.210 --> 00:05:45.480
I was wonder if we could geek
out a little bit on the car.

00:05:45.480 --> 00:05:47.430
Well this car was a fun one to build.

00:05:47.430 --> 00:05:50.010
So I spent the last two and
a half years designing it

00:05:50.010 --> 00:05:53.043
on a computer before we ever
started cutting the first tube.

00:05:54.870 --> 00:05:57.360
This thing really does have it all.

00:05:57.360 --> 00:05:59.430
An engine with enough horsepower to top

00:05:59.430 --> 00:06:03.180
150 miles per hour on
the desert straightaways,

00:06:03.180 --> 00:06:05.460
shocks that can basically
see what's coming

00:06:05.460 --> 00:06:07.230
before it hits you.

00:06:07.230 --> 00:06:09.420
A hardened underbelly to make sure rocks

00:06:09.420 --> 00:06:13.080
don't shoot up into a
fuel tank or your thigh,

00:06:13.080 --> 00:06:16.290
and Lidar and GPS to help
find that perfect route

00:06:16.290 --> 00:06:17.940
through the rocks.

00:06:17.940 --> 00:06:21.780
So as you can see, it says
Big Rock on the GPS right now,

00:06:21.780 --> 00:06:24.570
which is basically
describes the whole place.

00:06:24.570 --> 00:06:27.180
Still, even with all
the bells and whistles

00:06:27.180 --> 00:06:29.700
Jason has to put his
body through this race,

00:06:29.700 --> 00:06:31.350
like everybody else.

00:06:31.350 --> 00:06:33.420
What the is a LiDar when you're in the,

00:06:33.420 --> 00:06:34.920
I mean it looks insane, you know.

00:06:34.920 --> 00:06:36.020
It's full punk rock.

00:06:43.470 --> 00:06:45.210
It is brutal.

00:06:45.210 --> 00:06:47.340
It is, it is a pounding.

00:06:47.340 --> 00:06:50.010
I would get my kidneys to bleed.

00:06:50.010 --> 00:06:52.140
I would get blood in my
mouth while we were driving

00:06:52.140 --> 00:06:54.480
and feel it when I started
and I didn't think I

00:06:54.480 --> 00:06:56.980
was driving hard enough
unless I had that feeling.

00:06:57.900 --> 00:07:00.120
What Jason is describing is the law of

00:07:00.120 --> 00:07:01.860
Internal organs, which says,

00:07:01.860 --> 00:07:05.250
they tend to stay in motion
even after your body has slammed

00:07:05.250 --> 00:07:06.993
into rocks at high speeds.

00:07:08.100 --> 00:07:09.800
And that's just the physical part.

00:07:10.800 --> 00:07:12.017
Ooh, I love it!

00:07:17.542 --> 00:07:18.650
Oh, I love it.

00:07:18.650 --> 00:07:21.689
God, it's so hard to do.

00:07:21.689 --> 00:07:22.813
Ah, ah.

00:07:22.813 --> 00:07:24.810
Wasn't I like crying in there?

00:07:24.810 --> 00:07:26.850
You might be

00:07:26.850 --> 00:07:28.550
Ah, that's embarrassing.

00:07:29.760 --> 00:07:30.593
S-t.

00:07:31.980 --> 00:07:34.560
I thought it was touching, man.

00:07:34.560 --> 00:07:36.010
Man, that was funny though.

00:07:37.320 --> 00:07:40.223
One thing's for sure, it's
a hell of a rush, man.

00:07:41.130 --> 00:07:42.153
I need one more.

00:07:43.110 --> 00:07:45.360
I need to know that I was the best here,

00:07:45.360 --> 00:07:47.610
and if I never finish another one

00:07:47.610 --> 00:07:49.830
but I got one more win,
I'll be totally content

00:07:49.830 --> 00:07:51.120
And nobody's won four.

00:07:51.120 --> 00:07:51.953
Nobody's won four.

00:07:51.953 --> 00:07:53.190
Right, yeah.

00:07:53.190 --> 00:07:55.013
I want to be the first one.

00:07:57.240 --> 00:07:59.100
Hang around these guys long enough,

00:07:59.100 --> 00:08:01.323
and you too will start to feel the itch.

00:08:02.700 --> 00:08:04.293
Time to get my organs shook.

00:08:06.283 --> 00:08:07.210
Where did this go?

00:08:07.210 --> 00:08:08.700
Right there.

00:08:08.700 --> 00:08:09.556
All right, here we go.

00:08:28.680 --> 00:08:30.573
That is crazy, man.

00:08:43.800 --> 00:08:45.473
That's what I came here for.

00:08:47.040 --> 00:08:48.490
It makes no sense.

00:08:50.670 --> 00:08:51.503
It was awesome.

00:08:51.503 --> 00:08:53.193
It doesn't make any sense man.

00:08:54.300 --> 00:08:56.610
What? Like, like it's fun.

00:08:56.610 --> 00:09:00.823
It's but why would anyone do this?

00:09:00.823 --> 00:09:04.050
I was shaken, rattled and delirious.

00:09:04.050 --> 00:09:06.633
Just to say, can we do it again?

00:09:15.720 --> 00:09:17.033
I have good news.

00:09:21.782 --> 00:09:25.615
We have found the spot
where dreams come true.

00:09:29.310 --> 00:09:30.213
Now, you know.

00:09:36.210 --> 00:09:39.180
After the time trials, the teams regroup

00:09:39.180 --> 00:09:41.190
do some work on their cars

00:09:41.190 --> 00:09:43.323
and make their plans for the big race.

00:09:45.030 --> 00:09:48.070
Since I tragically did not
have a car of my own to fix

00:09:48.960 --> 00:09:50.883
it was time to explore.

00:09:57.180 --> 00:09:59.130
This is Hammer Town, where most

00:09:59.130 --> 00:10:00.543
of the onlookers stay.

00:10:05.160 --> 00:10:06.840
About a 10 minute drive away,

00:10:06.840 --> 00:10:08.763
just outside of the thick of things,

00:10:09.990 --> 00:10:11.853
there is Lasertown.

00:10:15.810 --> 00:10:18.780
It's where the, the riff
raff who want to get away

00:10:18.780 --> 00:10:21.123
from the riff raff come spend the week.

00:10:24.510 --> 00:10:26.853
There are people who
like King of the Hammers,

00:10:27.780 --> 00:10:30.990
and then there's Cody
who loves it so much,

00:10:30.990 --> 00:10:33.690
he decided to build his own private oasis.

00:10:33.690 --> 00:10:35.490
We actually have 40 acres now.

00:10:35.490 --> 00:10:37.190
Right next to the race.

00:10:38.640 --> 00:10:41.820
We are having a large fire,

00:10:41.820 --> 00:10:45.120
Friday night and Saturday night.

00:10:45.120 --> 00:10:47.610
So, if you guys are
around, or if you're not

00:10:47.610 --> 00:10:48.930
you can probably see it from anywhere.

00:10:48.930 --> 00:10:52.320
But don't call the authorities
if you see a structure fire.

00:10:52.320 --> 00:10:53.613
'cause it's probably us.

00:10:55.020 --> 00:10:57.180
It has everything a man in no man's land

00:10:57.180 --> 00:10:58.740
could want.

00:10:58.740 --> 00:10:59.573
Art.

00:10:59.573 --> 00:11:01.110
First. You got to play
with them a little bit.

00:11:01.110 --> 00:11:02.850
A koi pond

00:11:02.850 --> 00:11:04.983
That's Sunny, he's a pig.

00:11:07.680 --> 00:11:10.350
And of course a luxurious home made

00:11:10.350 --> 00:11:12.060
out of shipping containers.

00:11:12.060 --> 00:11:14.160
That's not what I expected.

00:11:14.160 --> 00:11:15.443
That's the point.

00:11:17.070 --> 00:11:17.970
There's even room for

00:11:17.970 --> 00:11:20.370
a couple hundred close friends.

00:11:20.370 --> 00:11:22.710
It's kind of turned into a
campground, we'll call it.

00:11:22.710 --> 00:11:24.330
Yeah, and, uh,

00:11:24.330 --> 00:11:25.680
Do you feel like, feed all these people

00:11:25.680 --> 00:11:26.790
or do they fend for themselves?

00:11:26.790 --> 00:11:27.623
No, they fend for themselves.

00:11:27.623 --> 00:11:29.543
They just, they, I just provide the dirt.

00:11:36.480 --> 00:11:38.340
They might be building cities from scratch

00:11:38.340 --> 00:11:42.480
these days, but to hear an
OG like Shannon tell it,

00:11:42.480 --> 00:11:44.790
things were very different
when the race first

00:11:44.790 --> 00:11:47.400
started back in 2007.

00:11:47.400 --> 00:11:49.350
I mean we started out
way back in the day, just

00:11:49.350 --> 00:11:50.400
rock crawling for fun.

00:11:50.400 --> 00:11:54.270
You know, friends going out
and hill climbing, and you know

00:11:54.270 --> 00:11:57.150
back then there was a whole
lot of alcohol and fun

00:11:57.150 --> 00:11:58.260
involved, but,

00:11:58.260 --> 00:12:00.960
This event has grown so much
from when there was a few

00:12:00.960 --> 00:12:03.270
of you guys around a fire, you know

00:12:03.270 --> 00:12:05.269
doing your own thing to now 80,000 people.

00:12:05.269 --> 00:12:06.102
That was,

00:12:06.102 --> 00:12:08.310
That was the good days when
it was just very simple

00:12:08.310 --> 00:12:10.380
and you know, you weren't out here for

00:12:10.380 --> 00:12:11.670
you'd show up for a couple of days

00:12:11.670 --> 00:12:15.060
for this race and now we're
here for two weeks and,

00:12:15.060 --> 00:12:16.230
I don't know how long you've been here

00:12:16.230 --> 00:12:17.520
but I'm ready to get the hell out of here.

00:12:17.520 --> 00:12:19.480
Right. Breathing dirt

00:12:21.840 --> 00:12:24.150
Sitting there the day
before the main event,

00:12:24.150 --> 00:12:27.083
Sipping a Bloody Mary
made by Bloody Mary Larry.

00:12:27.083 --> 00:12:27.916
Bloody Mary.

00:12:27.916 --> 00:12:30.690
Oh yeah, Bloody Mary Larry makes the best.

00:12:30.690 --> 00:12:31.590
Thank you Larry.

00:12:31.590 --> 00:12:34.620
Shannon's mind was on
his daughter and her car.

00:12:34.620 --> 00:12:37.110
She's tough, she'll get over
it, but I mean it kills her

00:12:37.110 --> 00:12:39.180
'cause she's literally been working

00:12:39.180 --> 00:12:40.680
on her car since the last race.

00:12:40.680 --> 00:12:43.500
Just, I mean, polishing
it, looking everything over

00:12:43.500 --> 00:12:45.720
you know, just anything she
can do to make it better

00:12:45.720 --> 00:12:47.790
and be perfect when she got here.

00:12:47.790 --> 00:12:50.507
And then you know, it doesn't
take anything to take you out.

00:12:50.507 --> 00:12:53.033
You know, it's, and we haven't
even got to the race yet.

00:12:57.092 --> 00:12:58.980
With the race approaching, it was time to

00:12:58.980 --> 00:13:01.320
meet some more contenders.

00:13:01.320 --> 00:13:02.370
I'm sometimes PG.

00:13:02.370 --> 00:13:03.300
I'll try to keep it PG Thursday.

00:13:03.300 --> 00:13:04.133
You don't have to.

00:13:04.133 --> 00:13:05.588
You can do whatever you want.

00:13:05.588 --> 00:13:07.144
Oh, we do it all.

00:13:07.144 --> 00:13:09.120
Oh, all right.

00:13:09.120 --> 00:13:10.290
The Gomez brothers are one

00:13:10.290 --> 00:13:13.560
of those teams that
make other racers sweat.

00:13:13.560 --> 00:13:17.313
There's Marcos, JP and
last year's winner, Raul.

00:13:18.210 --> 00:13:20.580
They operate a booming
tree clearing business

00:13:20.580 --> 00:13:23.070
in Northern California
and funnel a portion

00:13:23.070 --> 00:13:26.550
of their good fortune into
this ridiculous hobby.

00:13:26.550 --> 00:13:29.910
And all in for this
whatever week, 10 days,

00:13:29.910 --> 00:13:33.060
between the vehicles and the
team and just the living stuff.

00:13:33.060 --> 00:13:34.920
I mean how much do you
think it costs to be here

00:13:34.920 --> 00:13:36.150
for this race?

00:13:36.150 --> 00:13:38.280
So if you went to buy a car like this?

00:13:38.280 --> 00:13:40.173
You're spending 350,000, $400,000.

00:13:40.173 --> 00:13:41.214
350,000,

00:13:41.214 --> 00:13:42.047
400.000.

00:13:42.047 --> 00:13:42.880
Just to like buy one.

00:13:42.880 --> 00:13:43.713
Just to buy the car.

00:13:43.713 --> 00:13:45.063
Okay.

00:13:45.063 --> 00:13:46.080
The tire's $1,200.

00:13:46.080 --> 00:13:47.003
Yeah.
The wheel's $900

00:13:47.003 --> 00:13:48.600
And it, it just adds up.

00:13:48.600 --> 00:13:50.460
And, you're spending 500,000.

00:13:50.460 --> 00:13:51.540
To come do this thing.

00:13:51.540 --> 00:13:53.220
Yeah. Yeah.
Give it a go, Cool.

00:13:53.220 --> 00:13:54.100
A real competitive go.

00:13:54.100 --> 00:13:55.440
Yeah.
